'''weighting''' (wā′ting), ''n.'' [Verbal n. of ''weight''<sup>1</sup>, ''v.''] In ''coal-mining'', subsidence or other disturbance in a coal-mine due to “weight,” or pressure of the overlying mass of rock. A mine in which such subsidence is taking place is said to be “on the weight.” [Eng.]

